It is Friday evening and I am taking the U-Bahn home.
The train is very full, so I am standing.
My mobile phone vibrates.
I take the mobile phone out and open our badminton chat.
There are many new messages.
Timo asks who has time next week.
Max writes that he is on holiday.
Then Lena sends a photo.
It is a picture from the hall from yesterday evening.
I smile and want to answer quickly.
I hold on and type with the other hand.
I write my short message using only one thumb.
"I will play with you next week!" I answer.
Normally I miss my stop this way.
Mostly I only pay attention to the screen while typing.
But today I look up at exactly the right moment.
The U-Bahn stops and the next station is announced.
It is exactly my station.
I put the mobile phone away and get off.
